PROGRAM_STATUS:
On September 23, 2025, the City Council adopted Ordinance No. 6615 amending the Anaheim Municipal Code to implement clarifying technical changes required for full certification of the City’s Sixth Cycle Housing Element. The amendments modify Chapters 18.06 (Multiple-Family Residential Zones), 18.12 (Mixed-Use Zone), and 18.52 (Affordable Housing) to: 
(1) Allow by-right review of qualifying housing developments with at least 20 percent lower-income units on identified Housing Element sites; 
(2) Require a minimum density of 20 dwelling units per acre for certain sites when at least 20 percent of units are affordable; 
(3) Establish performance standards for mixed-use projects requiring residential uses to comprise at least 50 percent of floor area when 20 percent of units are affordable; and 
(4) Clarify eligibility for by-right review of sites carried forward from the prior Housing Element cycle.

